# _sys/boot scope 75 — auto-route hook (single-stack dev).
#
# This workspace has one app stack, `watch-mailbox`, so any HTTP request
# that didn't already match a hostname binding routes to it. That covers
# the two demo routes, POST /seed and GET /received, on a bare
# `curl localhost:8080/...` with no Host header.
#
# The mailbox the source watches is provisioned under the domain
# `pony.local.thanks.computer` (see the README): that hostname is bound
# to this stack too, which is what auto-verifies the domain so
# txco://imap/account will accept `desk@pony.local.thanks.computer`.
# When a request DOES carry that Host, detect-tenant@0 promotes the
# binding and this hook is a no-op (it only fires on an unrouted req).
#
# Production note: delete this file once you have real hostname
# bindings; path/host gating belongs in per-tenant routing, not the
# system bootstrap.
WHEN @route.to == ""
  && @src == "http"
  EMIT @route.tenant = "default",
       @route.stack = "watch-mailbox",
       @route.to = "watch-mailbox/0",
       @route.ingress = "auto-route",
       @route.hostname_verified = true
